					"documentation": "Scope: one group reservation, from request to confirmed places, refusal or expiry. Tour operators reserve provisional blocks. Ministry of Education representatives book schools. Payment settlement, QR issuance/validation, cancellation after confirmation and physical admission are separate processes. Confirmation here is of group size and allocated places, not proof of payment or permission to enter.\n\nSources: 00 Project Request: 30-minute capacity-limited slots; tour group blocks and final size confirmed 48 hours before visit, otherwise unconfirmed tickets released; schools through Ministry of Education, free weekday mornings. 02 Workshop: operator's 24-hour proposal is not adopted. Team requirements: FR-01, FR-03, FR-04 and FR-25. Assumptions: A-01 changes/releases, A-04 released slot capacity, A-14 school confirmation.\n\nEligibility includes authorised organiser identity, complete group/slot details, a positive whole-number count, a future released slot, and for tour blocks a confirmation deadline still in the future. Deadline = entry-slot start minus 48 hours. New tour holds and self-service size changes are unavailable at/after the deadline. No arbitrary group minimum is invented. A school booking must use the Ministry channel and weekday morning slot; A-14 confirms it immediately with zero price after capacity validation, without inventing the tour operator's provisional deadline for schools. Save the school, slot, count and confirmed status; the provisional confirmation deadline is not applicable to that school flow.\n\nCapacity checks count both confirmed allocations and outstanding holds. Recheck and allocate together to avoid overbooking if availability changes between display and commit; a failed allocation follows the insufficient-places path. Existing held seats belong to this reservation and must not be counted as extra available seats. Hall safe capacity is not this entry-slot setting.\n\nTour flow: save provisional block and deadline, notify operator, then wait for their final-size submission OR deadline. The wait does not require the operator to respond, and ends immediately if deadline already passed. The decision distinguishes a timely submission from expiry. Late submissions cannot revive expired reservations. Rejecting an invalid increase preserves the current block and loops back to the waiting merge; the original deadline is never extended. Validate positive integer size and remaining capacity for any increase and recheck deadline at confirmation commit. If final size is smaller, release surplus held seats on confirmation; if larger, allocate only the increase from available capacity. A zero-size cancellation is outside this final-size confirmation request. Invalid data can be corrected before the unchanged deadline, otherwise the block expires.\n\nThe diagram models one initial final-size confirmation. Further allowed pre-deadline size amendments use the same validation/update/release rule and preserve the already confirmed allocation if a later requested change fails; they do not turn confirmed seats into unconfirmed seats. No self-service amendments after deadline (A-01).\n\nExpiry releases only still-unconfirmed held places and not other bookings or confirmed allocations. Record expired status and notify the operator. Save confirmed size and adjust availability before sending successful confirmation. The two storage actions represent one consistent reservation update. Sequential notifications reflect dependent work; no artificial fork/join is needed. Separate activity finals denote alternative completed outcomes, never concurrent branches.\n\nBasic validation and safe concurrent allocation are requirements interpretations. A-14 is an explicit team assumption, not a museum statement. Notes carry details without turning them into additional executable activities. The organiser submits final size while the system's waiting action is active; this external event is described in the note, avoiding a mandatory human-response action that would incorrectly prevent automatic expiry.\n",
